I go to a fruit cart.
There are fresh yellow bananas on the cart.
There is a small cardboard sign there.
The price of bananas per dozen is written on the board.
One dozen bananas are for sixty rupees.
A young vendor is standing there.
I call him 'Dada'.
I say, "Dada, I want half a dozen bananas."
He puts six bananas in my cloth bag.
I ask him, "How much is it?"
He says, "Madam, thirty rupees."
I take out a large five hundred rupee note from my purse.
I hand the note to him.
I wait there and he counts my remaining money.
He gives me four hundred and seventy rupees.
I put the money in my purse.
I say, "Thank you, Dada."
I walk ahead in the market.
